Ok, folks!  Here are some spoilers that have been ardently requested.
Please note:  This is a work in progress and was taken from the pl6
source as they were the only ones I have access to.  If you have 
anything to add, please feel free to post additions/corrections, but NO
FLAMES!!

with that in mind, THERE BE SPOILERS AHEAD!!!!


I'm not kidding!

================================================================================
Assuming that you are in a normal state (NOT conf, blind, or halluc):

You can find out if an object is blessed, cursed, or mundane by dropping
it on an altar and observing the resulting glow (or lack thereof).
amber = blessed.
black = cursed.
nothing = uncursed.

================================================================================
My thanks to the dev. team's remarks for the following:

The list of musical instruments / effects is :

Flute			May calm snakes if player has enough dexterity
Magic flute		May put monsters to sleep:  area of effect depends
			on player level.
Horn			Will awaken monsters:  area of effect depends on player
			level.  May also scare monsters.
Fire horn		Acts like a wand of fire.
Frost horn		Acts like a wand of cold.
Bugle			Will awaken soldiers (if any):  area of effect depends
			on player level.
Harp			May calm nymph if player has enough dexterity.
Magic harp		Charm monsters:  area of effect depends on player
			level.
Drum			Will awaken monsters like the horn.
Drum of earthquake	Will initiate an earthquake whose intensity depends
			on player level.  That is, it creates ramdom pits
			called here chasms.

================================================================================
Many people have wondered what the code for the sinks was.  Well here it is.

Drop a ring down a sink and it gives a code as to what that ring was.

Effects that can be noticed without eyes. 

Searching:		"You thought your (ring) got lost in the sink, 
			 but there it is!"
Levitation:		"The sink quivers upward for a moment."
Poison Resistance:	"You smell rotten (fruit)."
Aggravate Monster:	"Several flies buzz angrily around the sink."
Shock Resistance:	"Static electricity surrounds the sink."
Conflict:		"You hear loud noises coming from the drain."
Gain Strength:		"The water flow seems (weaker/stronger) now."
Increase Damage:	"The water's force seems (smaller/greater) now."

Effects that need eyes:

Adornment:		"The faucets flash brightly for a moment."
Regeneration:		"The sink looks as good as new."
Invisibility:		"You don't see anything happen to the sink."
See Invisible:		"You see some air in the sink."
Stealth:		"The sink seems to blend into the floor for a moment."
Hunger:			"Suddenly, (object) vanishes from the sink!"
			[I'm not sure on this one, but it seems that several
			 items get deleted from your pack.  Please confirm.]

Fire Resistance:	"The hot water faucet flashes brightly for a moment."
Cold Resistance:	"The cold water faucet flashes brightly for a moment."
Protection From 
Shape Changers:		"The sink looks nothing like a fountain."
Protection:		"The sink glows (+/-/H)(silver/black/some color)
			 for a moment."
Warning:		"The sink glows (white/some color) for a moment."
Teleportation:		"The sink momentarily vanishes."
Teleport Control:	"The sink looks like it is being beamed aboard 
			 somewhere."
Polymorph:		"The sink momentarily looks like a fountain."
Polymorph Control:	"The sink momentarily looks like a regularly 
			 erupting geyser."

NOTE:  You have a 19 in 20 chance of loosing the ring, so don't do this 
       unless you have more than one.
================================================================================

On kicking attacks:

	(S)amurai and (P)riest(ess) get a random bonus damage on kicks
	based on their current dexterity.

	If (K)night and lawfull, unchivalrous attacks (from behind or 
	or defenceless) reduce your alignment from lawfull towards chaotic by
	one point per attack.

on kicking thrones:

	if your luck is bad (<0) 1 in 3 chance of destroying throne
	(0-200 gold pieces possible)

	if your luck is good (>=0) 1 in 3 chance of looting the throne.
	(300-500 GP + 1-6 gems) [only once per throne]

	You may also find a trap door.  (Fall through?)

on kicking altars:

	DON'T.  Bad things happen if you offend the gods.

on kicking sinks:

	80%	KLUNK!
	7%	Black Pudding Attack.
	4%	The dishwasher returns! Incubus/succubus attaks (Nasty!)
	3%	"Flupp! Muddy waste pops up from the drain"
		You see a ring shining in the mud. (if not looted).
	6%	Ouch!

